course: dictionary
lesson: 8583
title: Words about science
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scientific is an adjective. It can mean to do with science, or done in a careful, organised way, like a scientist. «The scientific method means testing ideas by careful experiments and measurements rather than trusting old books.» The clues are careful experiments and measurements, so scientific means careful and tested.
explain: Use the swap check. Put a simple meaning in place of the word, such as "careful and tested", and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Scientifically is the adverb. It tells you how something is done. A scientifically tested idea is one that has been checked in a careful, fair way.
fact: Scientific means to do with science, or done in a careful, organised way, using tests and evidence.
fact: A scientific method means asking a question, making a prediction, testing it fairly, measuring, recording results and reaching a conclusion.
fact: A scientific name is the special name that scientists give to a kind of living thing.
fact: Scientific evidence is proof gathered from careful tests and measurements.
fact: Scientifically is the adverb: «no one has shown real mind-reading in fair scientific tests.»
exercise: «The scientific method means testing ideas by careful experiments and measurements rather than trusting old books.» What does scientific mean here? | *Careful, tested, using evidence | Full of sound and music | Very old, from long ago | Happy and friendly
exercise: Mia reads that each new species needs a «scientific name». What is a scientific name? | A name for a pet cat | The name of a school subject | A nickname given by friends | *A special name scientists give to a kind of living thing
exercise: «No one has shown real mind-reading in fair scientific tests.» What do fair scientific tests use? | *Careful, fair checks with evidence | Only old books | Guesses and magic tricks | Loud music and games
test: The class followed the ___ method to find out whether plants need light. | *Scientific | Musical | Magic | Silly
test: Ella tested her idea ___, measuring the plants every day. | *Scientifically | Quickly | Loudly | Happily
exam: What does a scientific test mean? | *One done carefully, with a fair plan, measurements and recorded results | One done only once in a dream | One done by guessing, with no notes kept | One done for fun, with no rules at all
